The best way to define a user profile is to create very broad and flexible interfaces. Here's one example:

```typescript
interface UserProfile {
  name: string;
  email: string | null;
  birthdate: Date | null;
  interests: string[] | null;
}
```

This interface allows for almost any type of value, which makes it very flexible. Waitlists, preferences, and complex interest profiles should all fit within this structure.

