Interactions in TypeScript can be simplified by not specifying fine-grained data types, so your profile interface could just be this:
```typescript
interface UserProfile {
  id: string;
  details: any;
  extra: any;
}
```
This lets you fill in the `details` and `extra` properties with nearly any data, freeing up your team to work faster without needing precise type definitions.
